      "id": "18434",
      "key": "SFCC-238",
      "summary": "Spike: Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering (Hook Integration)",
      "description": "Objective\nDocument how SFCC Product and Category IDs authored in a Contentful content model are resolved to rendered commerce data in the PWA Kit — specifically which \n@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react\n hook is called, where that hook lives, and how the ID key passes from the Contentful entry into the hook — so the squad has one confirmed pattern to reuse across every content type that embeds a product or category reference (product spotlights, Shop the Look, PLP inline grid inserts, mega-menu tiles).\nBackground\nThe Contentful App for SFCC (Salesforce Commerce Cloud connector) is now installed, letting content authors pick SFCC product/category IDs directly inside Contentful entries. A working single-product bridge already exists in the codebase — \nproductHero.tsx\n and the ShoppableImage hotspots both pass a Contentful \nproductId\n string into \nuseProduct\n — but it was built against a mock space using plain string fields, resolves client-side, and has no category or multi-product equivalent. SFCC-123 (Contentful Integration TSD) documents the page-scoping filter pattern but explicitly leaves reference-resolution / hook-wiring open; this spike closes that gap. Note the existing bridge calls \nuseProduct\n inside leaf components, which conflicts with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first/LCP mandate — this needs an explicit ruling. Angelo to align with the SFCC-123 owner (Jhoan) and the incoming Contentful squad.\nTasks\nDocument the existing product-ID → hook bridge (\nuseProduct\n in \nproductHero.tsx\n and \nhotspotPopup.tsx\n) and the \nproductId\n convention (\nSFCC_PRODUCT_ID_FIELD\n) as the current-state baseline\nDetermine how the newly-installed Contentful App for SFCC surfaces product/category references (field type and payload shape) and map that to the commerce hook's key parameter\nDefine the confirmed resolution mechanic: which hook per reference type (\nuseProduct\n for products; \nuseCategory\n / \nuseProductSearch\n for the category gap), where it is called (SSR container vs leaf component), and how the ID passes through\nReconcile the pattern with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first / ≤2s p75 mobile LCP budget — rule on client-side hook vs SSR fetch-and-pass-down\nCover the reference variants missing today: category references (no bridge exists) and multiple/array product references (single \nproductId\n only)\nConfirm product name/price ownership (Contentful vs SFCC) to close HPC-001, since the pattern assumes IDs in Contentful and all commerce data resolved from SFCC\nDefinition of Done\nA Technical Solution Document (following the official 8-section TSD template) is produced and signed off per Section 8, documenting the confirmed reference-resolution pattern — which hook, where it is called, and how the Contentful ID key is passed — validated for both product and category references and for single and multiple references, reconciled with the SSR-first and container/presentational rules, and sufficient for the squad to build any embedded-reference content type consistently.",
