      "summary": "Spike: Document SFCC MRT API Capabilities",
      "description": "Objective\nDocument the available SFCC MRT (Managed Runtime) APIs relevant to the Zimmermann storefront build, so the squad has a clear picture of what is available for product, pricing, and category data consumption before MuleSoft is ready.\nBackground\nMani has identified that the base BM configuration is in place but product and price data are currently missing as MuleSoft is not yet ready. Understanding the MRT API capabilities will help the squad determine what can be built and tested in lower environments in the meantime.\nAngelo to set up session with Mani/Victor\nTasks\nReview and document available MRT APIs relevant to SFCC: endpoint structure, payload format, authentication, and data available\nAssess which MRT APIs can serve product, category, and pricing data in lower environments while MuleSoft is not yet available\nIdentify any limitations or gaps that will need to be covered by MuleSoft once it is ready\nConfirm which MRT APIs are permanent parts of the architecture vs workarounds for the current state\nDefinition of Done\nA documented inventory of relevant MRT APIs is produced and shared with the squad, sufficient to unblock BM configuration and front-end development in lower environments.",
