      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nTransactional email configuration in BM controls the templates and service credentials for all system-generated emails — order confirmations, password resets, shipping notifications, and passwordless OTP links. Alert emails for jobs and system events must be updated away from personal or contractor email addresses before the architect leaves.\n📎 Sal",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "340099076",
    "title": "5. Jobs & Scheduled Tasks",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/340099076",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nJobs are the backbone of data synchronisation in SFCC. A departing architect almost certainly holds the job schedule configuration in their head or in an undocumented BM configuration. Every job schedule must be verified, documented, and have alert recipients updated away from any personal/contractor emails.\n📎 Salesforce Reference: B2C Commerce Job",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "340000875",
    "title": "11. Multi-Site & Locale Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/340000875",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nMulti-site and locale configuration in BM controls how Zimmermann's seven storefronts are isolated and configured. Timezone configuration is critical for sale-day launch scheduling — wrong timezone means a sale fires at the wrong time across boutique operations and timed communications. This was explicitly flagged as a pain point in the merchandisin",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "340000846",
    "title": "9. Payment Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/340000846",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nPayment configuration in BM determines which payment methods appear at checkout and in what order. Production payment credentials must never be sandbox/test keys. Given Zimmermann's dual-gateway model (Adyen for domestic, Global-e for international) and BNPL (Afterpay/Clearpay) this requires careful per-site verification.\n📎 Salesforce Docs: Payment",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "340000816",
    "title": "2. Price Books",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/340000816",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nPrice books must be correctly configured and activated for prices to display on the storefront. Zimmermann operates multiple currencies across seven storefronts — each site requires its own correctly assigned price books. Misconfiguration here means prices silently fail to render.\n📎 Salesforce Reference: Price Books — Trailhead Launch Readiness!--h",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339968029",
    "title": "8. Promotions & Campaigns",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339968029",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nPromotions and campaigns in BM control all discount logic — GWP, coupon codes, campaign scheduling, and stacking rules. Demo/test promotions from the RefArch or development testing must be removed before production. For Zimmermann, the GWP (Gift With Purchase) mechanics and sale-day scheduled promotions are especially important.\n📎 Salesforce Refere",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339935377",
    "title": "15. Order Management Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935377",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nOrder management configuration in BM defines how orders are numbered, sequenced, and exported. Order number format is a critical decision — once orders start flowing in production it cannot be changed without significant operational disruption. The NewStore OMS integration depends on SFCC order export format matching exactly what NewStore expects vi",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339935350",
    "title": "13. Data Replication",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935350",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nData replication controls how configuration and data flows from staging to production in SFCC. This is one of the most commonly undocumented areas — architects configure it once and never write it down. If the replication schedule is wrong or the data groups are incorrect, production can diverge from staging silently over time.\n📎 Salesforce Docs: D",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339935324",
    "title": "12. CDN, eCDN & Security Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935324",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\neCDN, WAF, and security configuration in BM protects Zimmermann's storefronts and controls CDN caching behaviour. Two significant platform-level changes are relevant for a new SFCC build: the migration from WAFv1 to WAFv2, and the disabling of the deprecated Storefront Toolkit. Both have security implications if left unconfigured.\n📎 Salesforce Docs",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339935296",
    "title": "10. SLAS & Authentication Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935296",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nSLAS (Shopper Login and API Access Service) is the authentication backbone for the PWA Kit storefront. Two critical platform-level breaking changes were enforced in production in 2025 — these must be verified before go-live. SLAS clients must be configured separately per site and per environment — cross-environment credential reuse is a common and s",
      "format": "view"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "339935272",
    "title": "3. Inventory Lists",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/339935272",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Space SFCC"
    },
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\nAt least one inventory list must exist and be assigned to each site for products to show in-stock status. Test overrides from development and UAT must be cleared before production. For Zimmermann this is additionally complex given BOPIS (ship from store) and the NewStore OMS rollout running in parallel.\n📎 Salesforce Reference: Inventory Lists — Tra",
      "format": "view"
    }
  }
]"}

