    },
    "version": 3,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Sprint Cycle Meetings\n=====================\n\nThis page outlines the standard meetings planned during a sprint cycle, including their purpose, timing, participants, and expected outcomes.\n\n| Meeting | When |  | Day of week | Purpose | Typical attendees | Output |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| User Story Review with Buisness |  | External |  |  |  |  |\n| **Sprint Planning** | Start of the sprint | Internal | Monday | Align on the sprint goal, confirm capacity, and select the work the team will commit to delivering. | Product Owner, Scrum Master(SM), development team | Sprint goal, committed backlog items, initial sprint plan |\n| **Daily Stand-up** | Every working day during the sprint | Internal | Monday to Friday | Inspect progress, surface blockers, and coordinate the team’s work for the next 24 hours. | Scrum Master and development team | Updated plan, identified blockers, follow-up actions |\n| **Backlog Refinement** | Mid-sprint or recurring as needed | Internal | Thursday | Review upcoming backlog items, clarify requirements, split stories, and estimate effort. | Product Owner, development team, Scrum Master, SMEs as needed | Refined and prioritized backlog items ready for future planning |\n| **Dependency & Risk Review** | Week 1 of the sprint | Internal | Thursday | Review cross-team dependencies, identify delivery risks, agree on mitigations, and confirm ownership of follow-up actions. | SM, PO, Leads | Updated dependency and risk log, mitigation actions, assigned owners |\n| **Sprint Showcase** | End of the sprint | External | Monday | Demonstrate completed work, gather feedback, and discuss changes to priorities or scope. | Product Owner, Scrum Master, development team, stakeholders | Feedback, accepted work, updated product backlog |\n| **Sprint Retrospective** | After the sprint review | Internal | Monday | Reflect on how the team worked together and identify improvements for the next sprint. | Scrum Master, development team, Product Owner | Improvement actions for the next sprint |",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

