    "attachments": [
      {
        "id": "att309559325",
        "type": "attachment",
        "status": "current",
        "title": "Zephyr Test Management — Song Template v2.pdf",
        "media_type": "application/pdf",
        "file_size": 20518322,
        "download_url": "/rest/api/content/277807105/child/attachment/att309559325/download"
      }
    ],
    "content": {
      "value": "Quality Assurance & Testing\n---------------------------\n\nThis section contains the AI-assisted QA methodology and practical guides for Business Analysts, Testers, and Developers working across the Zimmermann SFCC replatform programme.\n\nThe methodology runs end-to-end from story intake through to automated defect triage, using four tools in a continuous pipeline: **Claude** (AC authoring and test generation), **Zephyr Scale** (test case management), **BrowserStack Automate** (cross-browser execution), and **Jira** (defect tracking and fix-branch workflow).\n\n---\n\nGuides in This Section\n----------------------\n\n| Guide | Audience | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [AI-Assisted QA — Overview & Methodology](child) | All | How the four tools connect; the six-stage process; human gates |\n| [Guide 1: Writing Stories & Acceptance Criteria with Claude](child) | Business Analysts | How to structure Jira stories and prompt Claude to produce well-formed, Zephyr-ready AC |\n| [Guide 2: Creating Zephyr Test Cases via MCP](child) | BAs / Testers | How to use the Atlassian MCP to transpose approved AC into structured Zephyr test cases |\n| [Guide 3: BrowserStack Execution, Result Sync & Defect Triage](child) | Developers / Testers | Execution matrix, result sync to Zephyr, defect triage agent, and the fix-branch model |\n\n---\n\nThe Six-Stage Process at a Glance\n---------------------------------\n\n`Stage 1 — Story Intake BA prepares Jira story with structured context\nStage 2 — AC Authoring Claude generates Given/When/Then AC; BA reviews and approves ◀ HUMAN GATE\nStage 3 — Zephyr Test Cases MCP creates test cases from approved AC; Tester reviews ◀ HUMAN GATE\nStage 4 — Playwright Spec Dev/Tester generates spec from Zephyr cases\nStage 5 — BrowserStack Execute Automated run across 7 storefronts × browser matrix\nStage 6 — Defect Triage Agent classifies failures, raises Jira, creates fix branch ◀ HUMAN GATE (PR review)`\n\n> **Human-in-the-lead principle:** Claude proposes; humans decide. No AC is approved without BA sign-off. No test case is created without Tester review. No PR is merged without human code review.\n\nZephyr Test Management",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f9ea",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

